 34S  c  J|p=0+ for {+32}S ground state (2025Ch19).                             
 34S  c  1978Cr01: a 10-MeV triton beam was provided from the Aldermaston tandem
 34S 2c  accelerator, United Kingdom. The target was antimony trisulfide. The   
 34S 3c  outgoing protons were analyzed in a multiangle magnetic spectrograph   
 34S 4c  and recorded in nuclear emulsion plates. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced
 34S 5c  levels, J, |p, and L-transfers from DWUCK-DWBA analysis. Partial work  
 34S 6c  on this measurement: 1973Cr04, 1975Cr07.                               
 34S  c  1979Fo17: theoretical discussion of the {+32}S(t,p)34S reactions.      
 34S  c  1978Cr01 states that since only relative cross sections were measured, 
 34S 2c  and since the absolute normalizing factor for a (t,p) distorted-wave   
 34S 3c  calculation is unknown, the normalization for the ground state has been
 34S 4c  chosen equal to 100. All configuration and normalization factors of the
 34S 5c  experimental to theoretical cross sections are given under comments.   
 34S  cL E,J,L$From 1978Cr01. The firm J|p assigned by 1978Cr01 is put in       
